The original code only checked whether the security level (encryption/authentication) was sufficient using `smp_sufficient_security`. However, it did not verify that the encryption key size is large enough for the required security level. According to the Bluetooth specification, the receiver of an L2CAP_LE_CONN_REQ must also check the key size and return `L2CAP_CR_LE_BAD_KEY_SIZE` if it is insufficient. The missing check caused the function to incorrectly accept or reject connections, failing the compliance test L2CAP/LE/CFC/BV-15-C.

